  "title": "International Committee of the Red Cross",
  "summary": "The ICRC traces its origin to February 1863, when a committee of five Swiss citizens, set up by a Geneva welfare society to examine Henry Dunant's proposals for the wounded, met for the first time in Geneva. That year it brought government representatives together, and in August 1864 it persuaded governments to adopt the first Geneva Convention. Its stated objective is protection and assistance for victims of armed conflict.",
